   "id": "nvidia-ceo-exit-earnings",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Chip stocks slide before Nvidia's first report since its CEO stepped down",
   "when": "Mon 16 Nov · US close",
   "what": "The Nasdaq closed down 2.49% and the S&P 500 down 1.92%. Reports say the chip index fell about 4.6% and Nvidia about 4.2%, after Jensen Huang left as chief executive. Nvidia reports after the US close on Tuesday; analysts expect revenue of about $109 billion. Anthropic's share sale is expected later this week. A new US rule also tightens China's access to top AI chips. Index futures were down about 1.9% (S&P 500) and 2.7% (Nasdaq-100) after the close.",
   "why": "Nvidia is a small direct holding, but the index funds and chip funds you own lean on the same AI names. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at 12 Nov; the S&P 500 is down about 2.3% since then. Their numbers will catch up in later NAVs.",
